  "body": "This stems from\nhttps://github.com/w3c/webappsec-referrer-policy/issues/53 and\nhttps://github.com/w3c/webappsec-referrer-policy/pull/66 which remove\nthe legacy keyword support from the HTTP Referrrer-Policy header. We\ninstead move that into HTML as a preprocessing step for the <meta\nname=\"referrer\"> element, before setting the resulting policy on the\ndocument.\n\nWhile there, this fixes the <meta name=\"referrer\"> parsing to align with\nChrome's implementation, as seen at\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/1348a36a3427d39554eab15e8920cec368829355/third_party/WebKit/Source/core/dom/ExecutionContext.cpp#239:\n- It includes the additional legacy translation\n  \"origin-when-crossorigin\" => \"origin-when-cross-origin\".\n- It splits the given value on commas and uses the last valid value that\n  is found, similar to what is done for the header.\n- It makes the search process use case-insensitive matching.\n\n@estark37, can you review? Also cc @jdm since I believe he was working on referrer policy in Servo and should probably be aware that we got the spec wrong for meta referrer for a while, at least compared to Chrome.\n",
